    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Verifies the Pax leap-year rule across a wide range of proleptic years. <p> Per the Pax calendar, a year is a leap year when the last two digits are divisible by 6, or are 99, or are 00 and the year is <b>not</b> divisible by 400. The test confirms that both {@link PaxDate#isLeapYear()} and {@link PaxChronology#isLeapYear(long)} agree with an independently computed expectation for every year from -500 to 499."
